{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/953502-garou-umbra-soak","id":953502,"title":"Garou Umbra Soak","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-18T17:25:11-07:00","id":953502,"title":"Garou Umbra Soak","content":"Ok, before there is a mistake I will explain that I had gotten rid of all my earlier WtA books years ago. Just recently gotten the W20 book, and have yet to get the W20 Umbra book. <br /> <br /> Am I missing something in the W20 book....I can't seem to find Umbra Combat for Garou. Or at least where it says how Garou Soak in the Umbra. From what I remember, Garou use Gnosis for Soak in the Umbra. Or am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:12:02-07:00","id":953535,"title":"","content":"You is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:14:47-07:00","id":953536,"title":"","content":"Then some elaboration would have been nice.....<br /> Garou use Sta like the Realm to Soak damage in the Umbra? If that's the case then seems Theurges are getting short changed, IMO","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 08-18-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:19:56-07:00","id":953542,"title":"","content":"In some of the early books, the game did have Garou soak using their Gnosis in the Umbra. That has long since (and by that I mean I think that was dumped before Revised came out) not been the case, and Garou always use their current Stamina + Armor if applicable to soak regardless of Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:37:01-07:00","id":953558,"title":"","content":"Thank you Heavy Arms for clearing that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:07:00-07:00","id":953568,"title":"","content":"Garou use their normal stats to soak in the Umbra, unlike the magi however - they use a different method which requires Spirit (or their Avatar Rating in case if they lack Spirit sphere) or something among those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:20:31-07:00","id":953616,"title":"","content":"Garou are half-spirits, so they get the best of both worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T21:40:21-07:00","id":953661,"title":"","content":"How mages soak in the Umbra is variable based on how they got into the Umbra, because they can enter in more than one way. But if they &quot;step sideways&quot; the way Garou do, then they'd generally soak with Stamina. Of course, Mages only soak Bashing naturally, and almost every spirit can do Lethal or Agg... so if they want to get into any fights they'll want some magic to help with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T23:51:39-07:00","id":953695,"title":"","content":"Actually, the rules changed right when revised came out.<br /> It was soaking with Gnosis in the 2nd edition (and probably 1st). Starting with revised it became Stamina (and applicable boni). However, the FAQ in the Storyteller's Handbook state that one could always use the older rule.<br /> <br /> The basic problem with Gnosis soak was, that Ahroun normally didn't have a good stat there, despite the fact that their mystical auspice is all about fighting and defending. So, using the same rules as normal combat seemed like a good choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T01:50:12-07:00","id":953718,"title":"","content":"I thought one of the later 2e books introduced the option before Revised made it official... but it's not worth digging into the library over it.<br /> <br /> It was also part of the frustration with the already imbalanced creation rules making Ahroun Lupus so popular, as Lupus means minimum 5 Gnosis, it was by far the cheapest way to make an effective Umbral fighter until the rules were changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:39:10-07:00","id":954066,"title":"","content":"Yes, I would have preferred a more point based system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:47:00-07:00","id":954072,"title":"","content":"Personally I will say in my own game, I go with whatever is higher, allowing the Theurge and the Ahroun the ability to shine against banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:56:32-07:00","id":954078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/953502-garou-umbra-soak?p=954072#post954072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I will say in my own game, I go with whatever is higher, allowing the Theurge and the Ahroun the ability to shine against banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea personally. It would also have the effect of a higher soak in non combat forms in the Umbra. Not sure yet how I feel about that though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:58:31-07:00","id":954082,"title":"","content":"Well I see it as a spiritual shielding, their spirit self is more resilient then their physical self, and it'd work that way regardless of form. Also since it only applies in the Umbra, its not like people aren't shifting crinos to protect the veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:23:06-07:00","id":954115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/953502-garou-umbra-soak?p=954066#post954066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I would have preferred a more point based system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have my house rules for balancing the splat Rage/Gnosis/Willpower spread somewhere if you'd like it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/953502-garou-umbra-soak?p=954078#post954078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this idea personally. It would also have the effect of a higher soak in non combat forms in the Umbra. Not sure yet how I feel about that though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stamina is going to win in most forms besides Homid anyway.<br /> <br /> There's also the kind of needlessly complicated soak rules to take into account. Remember that homids in homid, and lupus in lupus, don't soak Agg, which Bane's are going to use against Garou. Using Gnosis to soak doesn't inherently negate that. Which would keep this concern from really coming up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:28:37-07:00","id":954119,"title":"","content":"I would not mind seeing it, though please do not inconvenience yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T21:51:44-07:00","id":954199,"title":"","content":"Not really an inconvenience, since it's just finding one of my old threads here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages\"> House Rule: Balanced Starting Advantages - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37193-house-rule-balanced-starting-advantages </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I was asked to repost something I did on the old forums so here we go. The problem being addressed with the incredibly uneven levels of points you get by splat. A Ragabash Homid Glasswalker gets Rage 1/Gnosis 1/Willpower 3. An Ahroun Lupus Child of Gaia gets Rage 5, Gnosis 5, Willpower 4. For the </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T23:24:22-07:00","id":954249,"title":"","content":"I like it, Heavy Arms, and I almost wish we could sticky it here. These are some quality house rules, and I like how you discuss your methodology for assigning what goes where.<br /> <br /> It always did bug me that the starting values for will/rage/gnosis were either really high or really low depending on auspice/breed, and that to remedy this every player basically just bought their stats up (willpower and gnosis being in fairly high demand for most homid players, regardless of role). Your solution mitigates this problem and lets gives more texture to tribe choices also. Good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T02:27:51-07:00","id":954283,"title":"","content":"If I actually got around to posting more of my house rules, I'd probably just make a sig out of linking to them like Dataweaver does.<br /> <br /> Though we're kinda stretching the thread tangent. So I appreciate the positive response, but we should probably get back to the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T05:12:51-07:00","id":955528,"title":"","content":"To me this sounds like a good example of a Theurge gift. Question is what level is appropriate...<br /> Spend 1 Gnosis. For the remainder of the scene the Theurge can use his Permanent Gnosis as a soak pool while in the Umbra.<br /> Does not stack with various armor gifts such as Lunas Armor, Troll Skin, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:28:03-07:00","id":955780,"title":"","content":"Is that additive with their normal soak? If not... it's pretty weak. In most cases Luna's Armor would be vastly superior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T01:52:25-07:00","id":956211,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it is. I would say, that one uses Gnosis instead of stamina for soak, but allows bonus from gifts normally.<br /> Keep in mind, that in Crinos soak is increased by means of the stamina increase. So, ever garou in crinos has at least 4 dice to soak any damage. A character with average 2 stats, has 5. So, the gift would really only be of uses once you have 6+ permanent gnosis, so there is a benefit for the average theurge.<br /> <br /> If not the gift only is usable in areas where crinos isn't an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T02:33:00-07:00","id":956223,"title":"","content":"Sure, it's limited to 10 dice. But as i see it, not every Garou is a combat monster with 5 Stamina. This gives a physically weak Theurge a chance to survive some of the blows he takes in the Umbra. It's a decent lvl 1 or 2 Gift IMO. Probably something that can be expanded upon at lvl 3 or 4.<br /> Maybe a lvl 4 gift that gives you Gnosis x Stamina soakdice. Or make it a static, non-rolled soak that automatically removes damage equal the characters Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:03:11-07:00","id":956231,"title":"","content":"My issue is less the cap, but more than fact that most Garou are going to have a highter Stamina + form bonus than their Gnosis rating. A Stamina 2 Theurge Lupus fighting in Hispo has a soak of 5, which means they'd need Gnosis 6+ to even bother.<br /> <br /> For Metis and Homids it's the same math (Crinos or Hispo same bonus), but they start with significantly less Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Maybe let them replace their form bonus with their Gnosis if its higher? It's not as potent as just Stamina + form bonus + Gnosis, but since form bonuses don't generally change it will grow with the character and their Stamina instead of being at tension over which is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:15:20-07:00","id":956234,"title":"","content":"Or it could be Gnosis+form bonus. It is the Umbra and the Garou are suppose to be warriors no matter the Auspice. And there different forms obviously have different power levels. Just a thought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:19:46-07:00","id":956544,"title":"","content":"True, but it still puts the pressure on having very high Gnosis to be useful. Having it replace form bonuses (even +0 in homid) means it always has a chance to be useful even if certain characters will get more out of it than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T20:55:34-07:00","id":956760,"title":"","content":"To me only dumb Theurges don't have a decent Gnosis, and we are talking bout it being a Theurge Gift right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T21:42:03-07:00","id":956773,"title":"","content":"Considering the price of Gnosis, a lot of Homid Theurges are going to be awhile until they're in the 6+ Gnosis range. Gnosis is very valuable to Theurges, but being a Theurge doesn't guarantee you any more than anyone else. Having it be Gnosis + form bonus, is only useful when your Stamina is less than your Gnosis. Having to have Gnosis 6 to ensure it's useful (and Stamina is also useful, so there's little reason to skimp on it). And again, there's already armor granting Gifts out there. It needs to be something worth getting over Luna's Armor (as the closet comparison) esp. since Luna's Armor works anywhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}